उदक॑वन्त् a. furnished with water;
 f. उदकावती a
woman's name.

उदकार्थ m. ablution (lit. water-business);
 ˚म् to
perform and ablution.

उदगयन॑ n. the (sun's) northern progress;
 the time
from the winter to the summer solstice.

उदग्र a. having the top lifted, i.e. lofty, high, tall,
long;
 increased, excited, roused by (—˚);
 fierce, intense.

उदग्रप्लुत a. making lofty boundings;
 abstr. ˚त्व
n.

उ॑दञ्च् (f. उ॑दीची) turned upwards or to the north,
northern;
 n. उ॑दक् adv. northward.

1 उदन्त॑ m. end of labour, harvest, feast, quiet;
 news,
intelligence.

उदय॑ m. going up, rising (also = seq.);
 coming forth,
appearance, manifestation, origin;
 result, issue, consequence;
 success,
advantage;
 income, revenue, interest.

उद॑यन n. going up, rise;
 issue, end;
 m. N. of a king.

उद॑र n. (adj. —˚ f. आ & ई) belly, womb, cavity,
interior, inside;
 loc. within, amidst (—˚).

उदार॑ a. raising, causing;
 sublime, noble, excellent. m.
rising fog or mist;
 pl. the spirits of the fog.

उदर्क॑ m. breaking forth, sounding;
 result, consequence,
future;
 issue, end.

उद्दण्ड a. having a raised staff or stalk;
 raised,
extraordinary, sublime.
